  "id": "COMPOUND:41033 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between the compound [(E)-2-[(1S,5S,7R,8S,11S)-11-(2-methoxypropan-2-yl)-8-methyl-5-(2-oxopropyl)-4-oxatricyclo[6.3.1.02,6]dodec-2(6)-en-7-yl]ethenyl] 3-methylbut-2-enoate and the cancer cell line A2780cisR. This compound is identified as a target of multiple dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family members, which are known to play a role in various metabolic pathways. These SDRs are also targets of other compounds such as Erysimoside, Pseudopterosin Q, and 2-Methoxyjuglone, all of which are associated with the A2780cisR cell line. The consistent targeting of this compound by multiple SDRs implies a potential role in modulating cellular metabolism, which could contribute to the observed effects on A2780cisR cells. The evidence supports a mechanism involving the inhibition of metabolic pathways through the interaction with SDRs, which may lead to the suppression of cancer cell viability. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SDRs in the context of cancer treatment, though further studies are needed to confirm the specific mechanism and therapeutic potential.",
